Replace the upstream Coder promo card on the Getting Started page with --welcome-text

Upstream's getting-started.diff adds a "Next Up" card promoting Coder's own
commercial deployment platform (linking to cdr.co/code-server-to-coder). This
replaces that card's content with the existing --welcome-text value (already
used on the login page) instead, threaded through as a new welcomeText product
field. The card only renders when welcome-text is actually set, so this is a
no-op if left unconfigured. Same on/off gate as before
(--disable-getting-started-override), reused rather than adding a new flag.

To test: set --welcome-text "Some message" and confirm it appears in a styled
card on the Welcome page instead of Coder's own promo, and disappears entirely
with --disable-getting-started-override.

